      "writtenOn": "2019-05-14T12:55:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Apparently CONNECTIVITY_INTERNAL is enough to run the captive portal app. It\u0027s still slightly concerning but it\u0027s vastly less dangerous than MAINLINE_NETWORK_STACK, and more importantly the shell has it already (l.132).\n\nWhy do you need to add this at all for aosp/959832 ? The shell should be able to use ConnectivityManager#startCaptivePortalApp already thanks to its holding CONNECTIVITY_INTERNAL.",
